<title>BELGIUM: EU probes aid to Elf Aquitaine's Leuna investment.</title>
<headline>EU probes aid to Elf Aquitaine's Leuna investment.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission started a probe on Wednesday into subsidies received by French oil company Elf Aquitaine to build a refinery in Leuna in eastern Germany, a Commission spokesman said.  </p>
<p>&quot;We have started (investigation) proceedings,&quot; the spokesman told Reuters. There were no other details.</p>
<p>The decision forces the German government to provide long-sought information on whether Elf Aquitaine may have inflated the costs of building the refinery to claim larger subsidies.</p>
<p>Elf has said that the total cost was 4.3 billion marks. But the German press has reported that calculations by BvS, the successor to Germany's Treuhand privatisation agency, showed the real cost was over one billion marks lower.</p>
<p>The reports said Elf received about 1.4 billion marks in subsidies. -- Brussels newsroom 322 2876841</p>
